{
  "description": "The BTPS 1.2 event chain. `event` is sent by `envelope.from`; `named` is what the receiving platform holds of the event it names (`inReplyTo` on a withdrawn, `follows` on a proposal) between the same two parties, or null when it holds none. A withdrawn takes back its own sender's proposal (paid, partially_paid, disputed or refund_requested) while it is open; a proposal sent again follows a withdrawn. An implementation accepts every \"accept\" case and refuses every \"refuse\" case; `why` says what is wrong.",
